Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// This strategy tracks the visible output (`generated`), whether decoding is
// currently inside a constrained SMILES span, and the active constrained prefix
// (`currentConstrainedOut`). Outside a span it uses short unconstrained chunks
// so the model can naturally emit the visible opening delimiter "<<"; if that
// delimiter is observed, the strategy switches into parser-controlled decoding
// without appending a duplicate delimiter.
// Inside the span, the parser is the hard authority. The strategy measures how
// narrow the parser state is with `ValidTokenCount` and `DeadEndDetection`.
// When the state is narrow, it uses `AdaptiveConstrainedStep` with caller
// token-group preferences; when the state is broader, it uses
// `SafeRepetitionPenaltyStep` to discourage degenerate loops while still
// enforcing parser validity. If the constrained prefix becomes complete, it
// closes the visible span with `CloseConstrainedSpan`. This tracked state keeps
// the active SMILES prefix parser-valid at every committed constrained step.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In the outside-span chunk branch, `insideConstrainedOut`
